/// DYNAMIC ROLE: one role covers every manager, and adding a person is a row in
/// dim_security rather than a model change. USERPRINCIPALNAME() returns the signed-in
/// user in the Service. In Desktop use View as > Other user with a UPN from
/// dim_security, e.g. central.manager@journeyteam.com, ticking this role.
/// national.director@journeyteam.com maps to all six regions and so sees everything
/// without needing a separate role. dim_security is deliberately unrelated to the
/// rest of the model: the IN predicate reads it directly, so it never participates in
/// filter propagation and cannot create an ambiguous path.
role 'Regional Manager (Dynamic)'
	modelPermission: read

	tablePermission dim_location =
			dim_location[Region] IN
			    SELECTCOLUMNS (
			        FILTER (
			            dim_security,
			            dim_security[UserPrincipalName] = USERPRINCIPALNAME ()
			        ),
			        "Region", dim_security[Region]
			    )

	annotation PBI_Id = 1819a8702b2d4120bf8311211f3ae047

